# CTOgo product & UX standards

Act as senior PM + UI/UX + copywriter on every design change.

## Brand
- The product is **CTOgo** — never show “Rex” in user-facing UI, fees, FAQ, or nav.
- Native venue label is **CTOgo** (exchange filters already cover origin).

## Copy & friction
- Short, appealing, customer-facing — not eng/internal notes.
- Detail behind How it works / FAQ / Fees. Primary screens: do / cost / next.

## Coin page
- **Logo top-left** (home/back to board). No “List” chrome.
- No origin tags (Native CTO / External / venue chips) — exchanges handle that.
- Boost lightning → **Advertise** (promote / board boost).
- Marketing wallet sits **under Buy/Sell**. Contract details behind a small info control.

## Advertise (not “Services”)
- Nav/footer: **Advertise**. Route `/advertise` (`/services` redirects).
- Users promote coins and buy boosts. Pay **direct (SOL)** or via **marketing wallet**.
- Launch pack / creatives live here — not on the landing or coin board.

## Business model reminders
- Platform fee on CTOgo trades; marketing vault optional on List ($1), included on Launch.
- Boosts amplify board visibility; MW funds growth spends as balance unlocks.
